## (1) conservation world: the law's value per raw step and per question (bits)
#  m     g_0=log2(S/C)  g_{C/2}   per question: uniform{0..m}   iid Binomial (realised, |x|=m/2)   induced by raw no-law model at step t
     8       1.8707     2.6586           3.1699                 1.8707              = g_t exactly
    12       2.1483     2.9756           3.7004                 2.1483              = g_t exactly
    16       2.3483     3.1992           4.0875                 2.3483              = g_t exactly
    32       2.8370     3.7324           5.0444                 2.8370              = g_t exactly
    64       3.3314     4.2579           6.0224                 3.3314              = g_t exactly
   128       3.8286     4.7769           7.0112                 3.8286              = g_t exactly
  1024       5.3261     6.3080          10.0014                 5.3261              = g_t exactly
# chain rule: under RAW-NOLAW the step-t loss log2(S-t) = log2((S-t)/(C-t)) [the induced probability
# of the observed weight class] + log2(C-t) [the state within the class], and RAW-LAW's loss is the
# second term; so the law's raw gain g_t IS the no-law raw model's loss on the question 'what is |x_t+1|?'.
# identity checked at m = 12 for t = 0..C-1: largest |difference| 1.8e-15 bits

