# parametrisation of the prior box: halving the eccentricity ranges ([0,1) -> [0,0.5)) adds 1 bit of prior
# density per eccentricity element (the compatible regions lie inside [0,0.5) at every delta <= 120'),
# so it moves the vicarious hypothesis (two eccentricities) by 1 bit against the 4-element forms and the
# circle (no eccentricity) by -1 bit against them.

